  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run or build it here, so none of it has been checked in a browser. That includes the shader compiling and the first-frame `__EVAL_READY__` flag.\n\n- **Island:** A flat-shaded, faceted terrain is built from code as a 64×64-cell triangle soup. Each face has its own normal and colour, and the colour depends on height (sand, grass, rock, pale summit). The shoreline is irregular. About 26 low-poly pine trees and 14 boxy rocks sit on it, placed with a seeded random generator.\n- **Water:** A custom shader on a 150×150 grid animates the waves. It gives faceted shading, a fresnel mix with the sky colour, sun or moon glints, foam rings near the shore, and a fade into the sky colour at the horizon.\n- **Day/night:** A full cycle takes 20 seconds and starts mid-morning. The sun and moon lights move on arcs, and the `sky.preetham` sky (with stars) follows the sun. Sun and moon intensities and the hemisphere light are adjusted each frame, and the water's sky and light colours follow the same cycle. A hemisphere light stays on at night so the scene is never black.\n- **Camera:** It sits above the water at about [0, 17, 36], looks at the island, and orbits slowly through `interactions.orbit` with `autoRotate`.\n- **Light-intensity fallback:** Changing light intensity relies on `setLight`, which the typings mark as optional. If it's missing at runtime, the sun and moon switch on and off at the horizon instead of fading.\n\n",
